From d68b43782f79125b222e89eb3ba1f38cd8fa7f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigillus <nigillus@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Art pipeline: smooth ship sprites, asset checks, shot mode

- ShipArt: one loader for ship sprites (world map, shipyard, combat) with
  mipmaps + Linear filtering instead of three Nearest-filtered caches.
- Sprite edges bled (tools/art/art.py bleed): RGB under transparent
  pixels now matches the edge, so Linear filtering adds no white/black rim.
  Visible pixels are unchanged.
- tools/art/art.py: slice a generated sheet into named, trimmed, edge-bled
  sprites (reproduces the current ship2_* set to within 1px), bleed,
  preview.
- Source sheets and mockups moved from assets/ (shipped in the jar) to
  art-src/.
- AssetIntegrityTest: referenced paths exist, real transparent
  backgrounds, bled edges, no source files in assets/.
- Shot mode: --shot=<screen> opens a screen in a fresh game, saves a PNG
  and exits, so a visual change can be checked before the user looks.
  ShotRequest parsing covered by ShotRequestTest.
- art skill (/art) and an Artwork section in CLAUDE.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCeaxA1r43irxwHhesUMRp
